{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen","id":1533934,"title":"Gathering people's opinions about the God of Demon the Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-09T21:48:59-07:00","id":1533934,"title":"Gathering people's opinions about the God of Demon the Fallen","content":"I was a bit curious so if you guys could help me out<br /> so for the sake of the argument,let's say the cosmology of Demon: The Fallen exists in the World of Darkness just like the the cosmologies of the other games are assumed to co-exist (even though there are a lot of contradictions).<br /> let's also assume that while the cosmology of DTF exists in the wod,it is not the &quot;primary&quot; one,and it doesn't &quot;override&quot;other game lines' core assumptions<br /> What the god of Demon: The Fallen and it's angel actuallly are?<br /> are they umbral citizens?<br /> Are they the same god and angels who cursed Caine?<br /> I know there's no definite answer,but what do you think?<br /> are they related to the pure ones?<br /> Or to gaia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-10-2024, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T04:49:12-07:00","id":1533953,"title":"","content":"The Heavenly Host sort of has to be Umbrood in the broad sense because they're not native to the material plane; even if they predate the Umbra as well, most of the game's cosmologies allow for such a retroactive assignment for creator-beings.<br /> <br /> Who cursed the first vampire, and if the first vampire is even the Biblical Caine is mythology, not cosmology. I consider DtF making one of VtM's multiple creation myths &quot;officially&quot; the truth something that overrides another game line's core assumptions and is thus invalid.<br /> <br /> According to DtF the Heavenly Host aren't the Pure Ones or Gaia either, so in the opposite direction making them such would be violating DtF's themes.<br /> <br /> I think DtF works better with these as mysteries so the world the demons wake up to after escaping the Abyss is one they don't understand even on a cosmological level as so much has changed, and it helps maintain the premises of not having one game-line suborn the other(s).<br /> <br /> While I'm happy to entertain characters trying to classify newly encountered phenomena that don't actually conform to their preconceptions, I see very little value in trying to make them more than what they game asks of them to be: angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:00:22-07:00","id":1533965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1533953#post1533953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Heavenly Host sort of has to be Umbrood in the broad sense because they're not native to the material plane; even if they predate the Umbra as well, most of the game's cosmologies allow for such a retroactive assignment for creator-beings.<br /> <br /> Who cursed the first vampire, and if the first vampire is even the Biblical Caine is mythology, not cosmology. I consider DtF making one of VtM's multiple creation myths &quot;officially&quot; the truth something that overrides another game line's core assumptions and is thus invalid.<br /> <br /> According to DtF the Heavenly Host aren't the Pure Ones or Gaia either, so in the opposite direction making them such would be violating DtF's themes.<br /> <br /> I think DtF works better with these as mysteries so the world the demons wake up to after escaping the Abyss is one they don't understand even on a cosmological level as so much has changed, and it helps maintain the premises of not having one game-line suborn the other(s).<br /> <br /> While I'm happy to entertain characters trying to classify newly encountered phenomena that don't actually conform to their preconceptions, I see very little value in trying to make them more than what they game asks of them to be: angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>After giving it some thought,I agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T05:01:31-07:00","id":1534021,"title":"","content":"I like to think the Demon: The Fallen God is like or the same of the Kinderd of the East' <i>August Personage</i> of <i>Jade </i>the mightiest minsiter of the Heaven<br /> Actually this fits nicely with the &quot;fact&quot; the Scarlet Queen, also known as the Scarlet Phoenix, who one of the Ministers of Creation, the ruler of the Yang World and the Ebon Dragon the incarnation and embodiment of the concept of Yin. and rule or the Yin Word are - according to Lucifer - the last remaining Angels on Earth and they are probably the &quot;Messengers&quot; responsible for creating the imbued, or at least the leaders of the factions championing the virtues of Zeal and Mercy. As the Scarlet Queen represents Yang, the active principle, she would represent Zeal. The best of both principles were used to create the Vision creeds - as a kind of replacement of the defunct Wan Xian, theTen Thousand Immortals who failed their creators and became the Kuei-Jin<br /> Based on the lore of the Fallen, the Scarlet Queen is also identified as Ziana, the Seraph of the Cycle, ruler of the Sixth House of angels who is said to have become the World Tree, which may mean that she became Gaia.<br /> Back on topic, the Fallen are VERY similar to the Hsien (or Shinma) the &quot;little gods&quot; of the Middle Kingdom<br /> Once servants of the more powerful gods in the Celestial hierarchy, they were responsible for answering the prayers of mortals in accordance with the wishes of their superiors. During the terrible events of the Dragon River War at the beginning of the Fourth Age, and the fall of the Wan Xian in the Third, many Shinma rebelled against their position in the Celestial Bureaucracy, either to help mortals or turn against them. As a result, they were punished by the August Personage. Those who had dared to place themselves in the position of the Wan Xian were cast out and forced to live among the mortals of the Middle Kingdom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T11:14:51-07:00","id":1534035,"title":"","content":"The Ministers are most likely angels viewed through a different cultural lens (for all the problems that causes), and I would include the August Personage of Jade there (as the Ministers are not the Creator of All). Plus if you like the idea of each of the Ministers championing an Imbued virtue, the APoJ being the champion of Vision fits thematically and their being absent would help explain why the Vision Imbued went wonky.<br /> <br /> That said, the default assumption is that the Ministers aren't the Messengers nor did they create the power behind the Imbued. They reactivated the Messengers to start selecting new humans to Imbue after the Wan Xian failed lead the Creator of All to stop allowing new ones, and the beings that were tasked with selecting new ones were sealed. But as they were doing this without the Creator of All's permission or knowledge, and possibly intentionally, they reshaped the process and thus the Imbued are significantly weaker than the Wan Xian were. So it's harder for the Imbued to succeed like the Wan Xian did, but it's also much harder for them to fall like the Wan Xian did after they won their battles.<br /> <br /> Of course, who the heck knows how much of this would still be canon in a proper new edition of Reckoning considering that most of this stemmed from trying to use KotE and HtR as ways to make Exalted the &quot;real&quot; pre-history of the WoD and was left in for various reasons even after WW scrapped the idea of making the ties between the two games official.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T12:04:49-07:00","id":1534207,"title":"","content":"The actual equivalents of any real beings that defied the head of the Great Chain of Being and were cast down into hell are probably the Neverborn sleeping in the Labyrinth in Wraith. The demons of DtF, like any other Nephandic masters, are probably just the dreams of a Neverborn, or the collective dreams of multiple Neverborn, and are likely not any more &quot;actual&quot; demons than the demons of the Astral Plane or the demonics of the Tempest. Nor are they any &quot;less&quot; real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T15:51:35-07:00","id":1534216,"title":"","content":"That take, again, goes against the stated desire to not have one game override another. DtF PCs are not &quot;Nephandic masters,&quot; like some other beings in the WoD that share the name demon. Nor are they dreams of the Neverborn. They are fallen angels, thus actual demons by Christian cosmology (however many issues that causes). Anything that makes them not actual angels that actually rebelled against the Creator and fell, is invalidating to DtF's themes and premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T07:35:25-07:00","id":1534249,"title":"","content":"In my mind there would be a creator who created the triad as a conscious system to have the balance of life and death and the angels would be responsible for minor works, observing the creations and the passage of souls, but then the morning star's rebellion happened followed by Cain's curse, so the creator decided that his children needed to learn a lesson and therefore decided to leave them to their own devices, which generated the problems that came next, vampire clans, fomori, werewolves, changelings, mages and the fallen returning. The apocalypse would be a final test, if humanity couldn't overcome surviving the apocalypse then he would just erase everything and start again. Simple, but it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T12:17:06-07:00","id":1534262,"title":"","content":"hey guys,sorry for not being in this thread,i'll come backs soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T23:12:57-07:00","id":1534291,"title":"","content":"If any entity known to walk the World of Darkness' mortal plane has seen how the universe operates under the hood, it's the Fallen, who were the Creator's hands. Where the cosmologies of other games lines (mostly Werewolf) appear to exist outside of the modern Fallen's understanding, I reconcile the difference by choosing to assume that the Fallen's memories of the creation of the universe are compromised by the long ages spent imprisoned in Torment, or were removed from their minds as part of their punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T17:18:37-07:00","id":1534311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1534291#post1534291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any entity known to walk the World of Darkness' mortal plane has seen how the universe operates under the hood, it's the Fallen, who were the Creator's hands. Where the cosmologies of other games lines (mostly Werewolf) appear to exist outside of the modern Fallen's understanding, I reconcile the difference by choosing to assume that the Fallen's memories of the creation of the universe are compromised by the long ages spent imprisoned in Torment, or were removed from their minds as part of their punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is actually a background called legacy that allows you search in the memories of the fallen, there it is mentioned that the human mind cannot process all the memories of the fallen, only partially if you have the background. So basically that's the reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T13:19:50-07:00","id":1534368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1534311#post1534311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is actually a background called legacy that allows you search in the memories of the fallen, there it is mentioned that the human mind cannot process all the memories of the fallen, only partially if you have the background. So basically that's the reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>This also means that the religious grounding of the Fallen could be wrong, in whole or in part, and the human POV filtering it is adding in a structure that wasn't originally there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T15:18:36-07:00","id":1534373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1534368#post1534368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This also means that the religious grounding of the Fallen could be wrong, in whole or in part, and the human POV filtering it is adding in a structure that wasn't originally there.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the background, if you had 4 or 5 points you would remember moments before the Fall, you could even argue that these would be memories implanted or distorted by the human mind, but then I would also have to question whether the Garou actually know any thing about the triad, Gaia or the Umbra or if the mages really know how the universe works or is supposed to work, and that everything is just a delusion caused by their avatars. Anyway, this could start an interesting story, but it seems more like a hunter's conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T15:21:29-07:00","id":1534374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1534373#post1534373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the background, if you had 4 or 5 points you would remember moments before the Fall, you could even argue that these would be memories implanted or distorted by the human mind, but then I would also have to question whether the Garou actually know any thing about the triad, Gaia or the Umbra or if the mages really know how the universe works or is supposed to work, and that everything is just a delusion caused by their avatars. Anyway, this could start an interesting story, but it seems more like a hunter's conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, unlike D:tF, W:tA doesn't ever try to be a deliberate headscrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T15:33:46-07:00","id":1534375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1534374#post1534374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, unlike D:tF, W:tA doesn't ever try to be a deliberate headscrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just that they never stop to ask themselves how it looks from the outside. I would say more, but I would have to elaborate and it is not the focus here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T15:45:00-07:00","id":1534376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1534375#post1534375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just that they never stop to ask themselves how it looks from the outside. I would say more, but I would have to elaborate and it is not the focus here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the out of character text that doesn't lean on unreliable narrators to tell the reader how the world is? And furthermore, doesn't turn around and say that everything is still uncertain for any reason, where D:tF does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T16:04:27-07:00","id":1534377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1533934-gathering-people-s-opinions-about-the-god-of-demon-the-fallen?p=1534376#post1534376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the out of character text that doesn't lean on unreliable narrators to tell the reader how the world is? And furthermore, doesn't turn around and say that everything is still uncertain for any reason, where D:tF does?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking in the crudest way possible. Is it possible that the fallen are only seeing a scenario manufactured by human minds, so this has nothing to do with their origins? Thinking logically yes. Would this make a good chronicle? Possibly. The problem is that this would invalidate everything that has already been done because it was all caused by a mistake. A comparison with the Garou of WTA, would be if they were just a condition or a genetic anomaly (or disease if you prefer) and the stories about Gaia and the Triad were lies or folklore made by the Garou to justify their actions, they would soon go from being protectors to a murderous cult. Did you understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T18:32:00-07:00","id":1534381,"title":"","content":"It's kind of redundant to argue about cosmology from the D:tF perspective. The books canonize a kind of &quot;Layered&quot; reality, meaning they themselves acknowledge that they're either 100% on point or completely full of it depending on what reality layer you're on. This is highlighted in how they don't even understand that there are parts of the umbra beyond the lowest levels seen in Wraith.<br /> <br /> More on topic, &quot;God&quot; is any number of beings from an especially powerful umbrood, to a Gaia from a different angle, to Caine's father Adam depending on reality layer(Aka what source material you're using). There isn't enough coherent material to make a definite answer, and that's entirely by design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 04-18-2024, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T23:12:18-07:00","id":1534384,"title":"","content":"The original developer did make some claims that Demon wasn't entirely about Abrahamic religions. I'm not really sure that tack worked out or lasted for very long, but it was there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T11:00:50-07:00","id":1534399,"title":"","content":"It didn't last long enough to make it into the books?<br /> <br /> Part of the problem, is that DtF presents extremely Christian demons (and from that, not even broadly Christian based demons, but a specific view of demons from a small school of thought within Christian belief). If DtF demons worked more like Changeling where they actually did vary significantly by human culture, the idea that they're shaped by their human hosts would hold more weight. But atheists, Jews, Muslims, and followers of non-Abrahamic religions all get the same demons with the same cosmology and same loose memories of how things went down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}